# Dockerfile.windows — Windows x64 build via remote Windows machine
#
# NOTE: Nuitka does NOT support native cross-compilation from Linux to Windows.
# The --mingw64 flag is silently ignored on Linux. Wine-based approaches also
# fail because:
#   - Wine 8.0 lacks CopyFile2 (needed by Python 3.13 pip)
#   - Wine 9.x crashes under QEMU x86_64 emulation on Apple Silicon
#   - Windows containers only run on Windows hosts
#
# Windows binaries MUST be built on a real Windows machine. Use the remote
# Windows build script instead:
#
#   ./scripts/build-windows-remote.sh [VERSION]
#
# This file is kept for documentation purposes. There is no Docker-based
# Windows cross-compilation path.
